Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: romulus15: add audio playback over DisplayPort

The sound card has only WCD, WSA and VA links, so audio can't play on a
monitor attached to either USB-C port. The Romulus topology already
provides the DISPLAY_PORT_RX_0/1 backends and their mixers, and the
Surface Laptop 7 UCM profile (shared with the ThinkPad T14s) already
has HDMI0/HDMI1 devices. Those devices only appear once the machine
driver creates the DP0/DP1 jacks, which needs these DAI links.

Follows the Surface Pro 11 patch "arm64: dts: qcom: x1-denali: Add
audio playback over DisplayPort" on the same SoC.
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus15.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus15.dts
index c9ce9c61a..e1b1b784b 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus15.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus15.dts
@@ -16,3 +16,42 @@
 #include "x1e80100-microsoft-romulus15-touchscreen.dtsi"
 
 #include "x1e80100-microsoft-romulus15-gpio-power.dtsi"
+
+/*
+ * Both USB-C ports carry DisplayPort (DP0, DP1). The Romulus topology already
+ * has the DISPLAY_PORT_RX backends; these links give the machine driver the
+ * "DP0 Jack"/"DP1 Jack" controls that UCM's HDMI0/HDMI1 devices need.
+ */
+&{/sound} {
+	displayport-0-dai-link {
+		link-name = "DisplayPort0 Playback";
+
+		codec {
+			sound-dai = <&mdss_dp0>;
+		};
+
+		cpu {
+			sound-dai = <&q6apmbedai DISPLAY_PORT_RX_0>;
+		};
+
+		platform {
+			sound-dai = <&q6apm>;
+		};
+	};
+
+	displayport-1-dai-link {
+		link-name = "DisplayPort1 Playback";
+
+		codec {
+			sound-dai = <&mdss_dp1>;
+		};
+
+		cpu {
+			sound-dai = <&q6apmbedai DISPLAY_PORT_RX_1>;
+		};
+
+		platform {
+			sound-dai = <&q6apm>;
+		};
+	};
+};
